---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
title="Making a website — Mike Trounce"
description="A few different ways I've built websites for clients."
>
<div class="options-page">
<a href="/" class="back-link">&larr; Mike Trounce</a>

<h1>Making a website</h1>
<p class="intro">
A few different routes I've taken for clients, depending on budget, how much the site needs to do, and how often it'll change.
</p>

<section class="project">
<h2>Wix Light — The Greensman</h2>
<p class="project-meta">£9/month &middot; Elstead, Surrey</p>
<p>
<a href="https://www.thegreensmanelstead.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">thegreensmanelstead.com</a> is the site for Freddy Trounce's garden maintenance business. I took over an existing Wix build, already on the paid Light plan (£108/year) plus the domain (£17/year) — set up and paid for by the original developer, likely as much in exchange for gardening work as for cash. We're now moving the site to a self-hosted setup, which will save Freddy over £100 a year, starting next year.
</p>
</section>

<!-- Add further <section class="project"> blocks here as more examples come in -->
</div>
</Layout>

<style>
.options-page {
  max-width: 640px;
  margin: 0 auto;
  padding: 4rem 1.5rem 6rem;
  color: var(--ink);
}

.back-link {
  display: inline-block;
  margin-bottom: 3rem;
  color: var(--ink-soft);
  text-decoration: none;
  font-size: 0.9rem;
}

.back-link:hover {
  color: var(--accent);
}

h1 {
  margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
}

.intro {
  color: var(--ink-soft);
  margin: 0 0 3rem;
}

.project {
  padding: 1.75rem 0;
  border-top: 1px solid var(--illus-b);
}

.project h2 {
  margin: 0 0 0.25rem;
  font-size: 1.15rem;
}

.project-meta {
  margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
  color: var(--ink-soft);
  font-size: 0.85rem;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  letter-spacing: 0.02em;
}

.project a {
  color: var(--accent);
}
</style>
